cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these datasets, please cite them using the metadata below."
type: dataset
title: "huspm-datasets: quantitative sequence databases for high-utility sequential pattern mining"
abstract: >
  Quantitative sequence databases used across several high-utility sequential
  pattern mining studies, so that each measures on exactly the same bytes. The
  sequence structure comes from the public SPMF datasets, which carry no
  utilities; internal quantities and external profits are generated
  deterministically by SPMF_Converter with a fixed seed and a per-file random
  stream, so a given raw file converts to the same bytes regardless of what else
  is converted alongside it. Each release ships a tarball and a SHA-256 manifest
  so a study can pin the exact data it measured on.
